LOK: Calc changes sheets, rows, columns and merges by address

- .uno:ElyStructure (Verb, Address, Value) runs one structure verb on
  the sheet the address names, through ScDocFunc, so the cursor,
  selection and shown sheet stay; each is one undo step:
  sheet.add (Address = name, Value = position from 1 or empty for last),
  sheet.remove, sheet.rename (Value = new name), rows.insert,
  rows.delete, columns.insert, columns.delete (Sheet1!5:7, Sheet1!C:E),
  rows.height, columns.width (Value = twips or "auto"), range.merge
  (hidden cells keep their contents), range.unmerge.
- sheet.freeze (Address = one cell) sets the sheet's LOK freeze above
  and left of the cell, as FreezePanesColumn/Row do under LOK; A1
  unfreezes. Like Calc's own freeze it is not an undo step.
- .uno:StructureAt?verb=&address=&value= answers the same verb's
  refusal before anything changes: "sheet" (no such sheet), "protected",
  "name", "taken", "position" (with "last"), "last" (the only visible
  sheet), "address", "edge" (insert pushes content off the sheet),
  "size", "single", "merged", "unmerged"; or the range it takes.
- .uno:SheetsAt lists every sheet's name, used area (left out when
  empty) and whether it is hidden.

